{title: Bless the Lord, My Soul}
{subtitle: Psalms 103:19–22}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm] | [Abmaj7] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The wind passes over [Bb]it and is [Cm]gone
Its place knows it [Ab]no more now
[Eb]But steadfast love rests from [Bb]everlasting
[Cm]On those who fear [Ab]the name
[Eb]His righteousness abides on [Bb]children's children
[Cm]Those who keep the co[Ab]venant
Remem[Eb]bering to obey his [Bb]precepts
[Cm]With faithfulness and [Ab]devotion
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Bless the Lord you mighty [Bb]angels
Do his word and obey his [Cm]voice
Bless the Lord all his [Ab]hosts
Servants who do his [Eb]will
Bless the Lord all his [Bb]works
In every place of his domin[Cm]ion
Bless the [Ab]Lord my [Eb]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He has established his [Bb]throne in the heavens
[Cm]His kingdom rules over [Ab]all things
[Eb]The Lord is high and ex[Bb]alted
His [Cm]glory fills the [Ab]world
From the [Eb]depths to the highest [Bb]sky
His dominion stands firm
[Cm]His word is the voice of pow[Ab]er
Guiding every step [Eb]we take
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Bless the Lord you mighty [Bb]angels
Do his word and obey his [Cm]voice
Bless the Lord all his [Ab]hosts
Servants who do his [Eb]will
Bless the Lord all his [Bb]works
In every place of his domin[Cm]ion
Bless the [Ab]Lord my [Eb]soul
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
His love endures forev[Bb]er
For those who [Cm]fear him
His [Ab]righteousness is sure
For their [Eb]children's children
Keep his [Bb]covenant true
Remem[Cm]ber his precepts
His [Ab]kingdom never fades
His throne is in [Eb]the heavens
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Bless the Lord you mighty [Bb]angels
Do his word and obey his [Cm]voice
Bless the Lord all his [Ab]hosts
Servants who do his [Eb]will
Bless the Lord all his [Bb]works
In every place of his domin[Cm]ion
Bless the [Ab]Lord my [Eb]soul [Bb][Cm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Abmaj7]Bless the [Eb]Lord my [Bb]soul
Bless the [Cm]Lord my [Abmaj7]soul
